{"title":"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two-thirds of the people in a room are seated in three-fourths of the chairs. The rest of the people are standing. If there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> empty chairs, how many people are in the room?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/c/44cf037de1f6cdb7f6dc080da681194a3b79ea14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 12\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 18\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 24\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 27\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Working backwards, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/c/2bcddca5092a7ec886294a0561a3f69b682f12d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> of the chairs are taken and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are empty, then there are three times as many taken chairs as empty chairs, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/233d3e7a52176d110ae5a4f7ee899fcb652a0034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 6 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is the number of people in the room and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/b/38bd36e353df831303c0de895a9ec614cf3e7202.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> are seated, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fc7b03eb5ff03ac2633e08faba468e092823690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac23 x = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd3d207caa54335e854a80fddc21d7902db947ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{(\\text{D}) 27}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"91\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8\">2004 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;